From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: TB321FU DSC width rounding

From GUF296's TB321FU-7.1.1 tree: round the DSC-compressed timing width up
instead of truncating.

The companion GUF change that skipped the first primary SSPP programming
after a display resume is dropped: on 7.2 the SSPP registers are zero after
the DPU power-collapses, so skipping that commit makes the pipe fetch from
IOVA 0, the corrupted DSC stream desyncs the panel decoder and the whole
screen shows noise until the panel is re-initialised.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c	2026-09-28 11:21:42.733821828 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c	2026-09-28 11:21:42.807495871 +0200
@@ -134,8 +134,9 @@
 		 * TODO: replace drm_dsc_get_bpp_int with logic to handle
 		 * fractional part if there is fraction
 		 */
-		timing->width = timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) /
-				(dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
+		timing->width = DIV_ROUND_UP(timing->width *
+					     drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc),
+					     dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
 		timing->xres = timing->width;
 		timing->dce_bytes_per_line = msm_dsc_get_bytes_per_line(dsc);
 	}
